Z||000000||WhiteFieroBlur||05-31-2000||10:28 AM|||| I was looking thru posts and found the thread about making your turn signal lights move from side to side. Here is where I saw it at <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000771.html." TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000771.html.</A> <BR>    I was wondering if anyone finally found out how to do it without buying the expensive kit or if there is a kit someone found that doesn't cost so much. Also if you got the kit, is it really easy to install and is it just better to go ahead and buy the kit? And can this be done on all the year and model cars?<P>  Also I wanted to know how to make my license plate light look bright with a certain color. I put in purple recently and it still shines white on the plate. I used 194B auto bulbs.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Greg Piet||05-31-2000||12:12 PM||||I built one that works on my notchback<BR>the folowing site has a schematic and a pdf file to make your own circuitboards <A HREF="http://www.physics.unlv.edu/~gregpiet/Fiero1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.physics.unlv.edu/~gregpiet/Fiero1.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||lawrence||05-31-2000||12:54 PM||||I sell a kit for $59.95, and it's the lowest priced kit I've seen on the internet.  I've sold dozens of kits for Fieros and probably 10 or more other cars.  See some of the Club Members at:<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/sts/stsclub.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/sts/stsclub.htm</A> <P>I've even sold a kit to a guy with a Peterbuilt (still waiting for a pic).<P>The major advantage of my kit is that it allows you to chose between normal brake light action (no sequencing when you apply the brakes) or sequencing of the brake lights.<P>If you want to know how to install the kit, I have Fiero specific instructions here:<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/sts/stsfiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/sts/stsfiero.htm</A> <P>Of course, I'd like you to buy a kit from me, but if you'd rather build a set of modules yourself, I have the schematic available at:<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/99/3/we.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/99/3/we.htm</A> <P>Good luck,<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe</A>  - WebElectric Magazine<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Patrick||05-31-2000||01:58 PM||||<BR>The link in the first post does not work because there is a period on the end of it. This link should work:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000771.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000771.html</A> <P>When I started the original thread, I had no idea that anyone else would be interested. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||WhiteFieroBlur||05-31-2000||04:49 PM||||Thanx for the info I am gonna look at it and see if I can do it myself but if its way too hard I think I'll just get that kit for 59 dollars :O). <P> Has everyone been pleased with the way the lights turned out? And do you get alot of attention with lights like that? I don't think anyone here has even heard of a thing like that with your lights around here. But I am sure we are all used to people beaing baffled about our car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. I got another victim Monday at our Bar B Que with him scratching his head and saying, "The engines in the back??!!"||||reg||1
Z||000005||DiggityDan||05-31-2000||04:52 PM||||Lawrence, I ran across your site the other day. Nice work. I'm a little too dumb I guess to make the circuitry you are talking about but I am interested in the sequential turn signals and the one touch power windows. What would a "special" combo price run for both? You make the kits, packed some instructions into the box for us - or me - layman to install the circuitry into the cars, you get a nice check in return. Would that work for you?||||reg||1
Z||000006||lawrence||05-31-2000||09:00 PM||||DiggityDan,<P>Sorry, but I don't sell a kit for the one-touch windows -- the current sensors are time consuming to make and require a bit of adjusting since each car is slightly different.<P>For the Sequentials, I'll offer the same "Club Discount" that I give others.  If you put together a purchase of 5 or more kits, you can deduct 10%.  Ten or more kits, and deduct 15%.  All kits must be shipped to the same address.<P>-L <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/sts" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/sts</A>  - Sequential Turn Signals||||reg||1
Z||000007||DiggityDan||06-01-2000||02:09 AM||||Well, I was really looking forward to those one touch windows, I guess I will try and find a buddy to do it for me. I am all for the group purchase on the turn signals. <BR>If anyone else is interested, e-mail me and we can see if we can set something up.||||reg||1
Z||000008||lawrence||06-01-2000||08:34 PM||||There's a guy named Oliver that has built a one-touch unit that works similar to mine, but it a completely different design.  Perhaps he is ready to sell them.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/fieroidx.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/fieroidx.html</A> <P>Send him an email, I know he will return your message.<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe</A>  - WebElectric Magazine||||reg||1
